Let $D$ be a finite simply connected union of triangles with simple polygonal boundary, and let $a$ be a boundary port. If $W(\gamma)$ is the total signed turning of a path, measured from its inward initial direction to its outward final direction, then $$\label{eq:01-boundary-identity}
 \sum_{b\in\partial D}\ \sum_{\gamma:a\to b}
       \rho^{|\gamma|}e^{itW(\gamma)}=1.$$ If $D$ is convex, its unsigned boundary partition sum is at most $1/c$.

Let $\eta=2d-1$ and $$\label{eq:01-g-definition}
 g_X(z)=\frac{p_{N+1}(a_1,\ldots,a_N,z)}{p_N(a_1,\ldots,a_N)}.$$ Then $g_X$ is monic of degree $N$ for generic $X$, and $$\label{eq:01-arch-formula}
